{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/724170-strix-on-tv","id":724170,"title":"Strix on TV","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-24T14:43:51-07:00","id":724170,"title":"Strix on TV","content":"Last episode of The Originals (I can't be the only one watching it) had the new bad guy drop a card with an owl on it. Turns out she works for the oldest vampire organization, The Strix. Also, on American Horror Story, someone took a picture of a vamp(?) and his face was blurred. Is Requiem creeping into the mainstream?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T15:24:55-07:00","id":724269,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://vampirediaries.wikia.com/wiki/The_Strix\" target=\"_blank\">Well, that's a thing</a>. Surprising...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T18:57:55-07:00","id":724730,"title":"","content":"It's not new. As nocturnal creatures that eat carrion and blood, owls have long been associated with death and misfortune, which go hand in hand with vampires. And it used to be a common trope that vampires didn't cast a reflection because they had no soul. As for AHS, they've been deliberately coy about the reflection thing with their depiction of vampires. Reflective surfaces everywhere but the poor lighting and distorted surface area would make seeing a clear reflection difficult. Apparently Elizabeth has a fascination with turning actors and models into vampires but it's not specific to whether or not those careers were maintained afterwards. Scarlett took Holden's picture right as he was moving in to bite her but when she looked at him he immediately withdrew, so his image could have blurred due to his movement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 10-24-2015, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T19:10:28-07:00","id":724744,"title":"","content":"Well, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strix_(mythology)\" target=\"_blank\">they didn't exactly come from Requiem.</a><br /> <br /> But I am of the belief that at least some writers for these paranormal shows or books take some concepts from rpgs, who really tend to make figuring out backgrounds and 'mechanics' easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T00:32:04-07:00","id":725327,"title":"","content":"A year after Changeling the Lost there was <i>Lost Girl</i>. I think everyone writing in the genre builds off everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T02:43:12-07:00","id":725451,"title":"","content":"And in True Blood Season 5 we got to see a council of vampires that kind of reminded me of the inner circle of the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T04:36:21-07:00","id":725566,"title":"","content":"The Southern Vampire Mysteries have a kind of V:tM feel, which carried over to some extent to True Blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T07:02:25-07:00","id":725848,"title":"","content":"I'll add to the presence of owls as demonic entities in genre fiction. Twin Peaks had owls as malicious spirits that possessed bodies to go on wanton murder sprees, and Batman introduced the idea of the Court of Owls, a malevolent secret society rumored to be immortal that utilized a brainwashed army of super assassins not that dissimilar from VII.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's a case of writers copping their material from WoD books so much as creatives in various mediums drawing from similar source materials. That said, I wouldn't be surprised to hear some of these genre writers are roleplayers. George R.R. Martin is well known for adapting his game sessions into novels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T08:31:47-07:00","id":726073,"title":"","content":"They also have a lot of owl motifs in Gravity Falls, though that is just a reference to Twin Peaks. Still, it's been pointed out that bill cipher's personality is very strix-like.<br /> <br /> and there is a stealth game called DARK (by the same people that made Tropico) that uses the term Vitae to describe the blood in a vampire's system used to fuel abilities and has several points where the player character commits diablerie (though they don't call it that) to avoid regressing into what's basically a dragur (due to the botched nature of his embrace). That being said, the game's pretty bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 10-25-2015, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}